insert_before('- **THE `new Date(...)` UTC OFF-BY-ONE (V203', OPEN.rstrip('\n').split('\n') + [''], 'section 12 V204 adds')

# ── ELEMENT 6 — ONE digest line, newest first ────────────────────────────────
DIGEST = r"""- **V204 — the clock that printed `7:60`, and the three gates that computed `7:60` too.** Mario, off his own card: a pace reading **`7:60/mi`** on a card whose `dose.tgt` was the correct **480**. The number was right and only the string was wrong — eleven formatters split the minutes off a fractional pace and THEN rounded the remainder, and `round(59.5)` is `60`. **D126** makes `_clkMS(sec)` the single owner of every seconds limb: round the whole value, then split, so `:60` is structurally impossible rather than corrected after the fact. Mario ruled **"fix the whole family"** over the cheaper one-formatter option, because six of the copies are fed by logged or wizard data whose domains were never measured and the next occurrence would surface where it is hardest to see. **Eleven** copies re-pointed; the **twelfth** (`applySeedData`) left alone, already carrying its own `ss===60` carry. Before: **264 malformed strings across 3,152,159 scanned card fields**, all on the pace-goal path; after: **0** on the run build path, plus 0 by direct probe on the three log-and-wizard-fed formatters a build sweep cannot reach. Pre-existing, and it had MOVED: **628** occurrences at one shape on V201 (advanced only), **264** across eight shapes and intermediate too after V202's run-path rework, byte-identical on V203. **The gate half was the real finding.** Three gates had copied the defective idiom into their own oracles (`g203_ceiling_and_anchor.js:91`, `g202_pace_anchor.js:47`, `g202_int_doctrine.js:64`) and were computing `7:60` on both sides of the comparison; **twelve read-back regexes used `\d\d` for a seconds limb**, including the `toSec` PARSER, which silently **normalised `7:60` to 480 s** so every downstream arithmetic assertion passed on text that was not a time. All corrected — and correcting them **changed nothing**: the gates still passed on V203, because **659 oracle invocations saw 0 fractional inputs** and **62 lattice configs / 104,822 strings held 0 malformed seconds**. The blindness never had to work. The real cause was a **LATTICE COVERAGE GAP**, closed with one named fractional row (**6:46 mile anchor, seed 76308**) that takes `g202_int_doctrine` to **27/0** on the candidate and **23/4 on V203** — the gate can now fail on the defect it was fixed for. New `tests/gates/g204_clock_limb.js` (**31** rows at first cut, **65** after one wiring row per formatter plus a source census, which is how the two whole-second-domain formatters get honest coverage) and `tests/measure/v204_idiom_census.js`, whose masker **parses its own masked output as a self check** so a desynced scan cannot produce the counts. Sabotage **6/6**. `HALF_MANNY` **UNMOVED** at `7d4f7ed45cc5bd53`, all three era tables carrying `[204]` REFERENCE rows verified by rebuilding each arm against the V203 literals. **The session's own process failure, recorded not smoothed over:** the orchestrator issued **D126** for the formatter **while coach was mid-ruling** on run-day lift placement, and coach's ruling took D126 as well; it became **D127** and the registry line moved in the same edit — the fifth collision in this file. Mario's challenge to the proposed pace-goal week (*"hinge and heavy lift before another LSD day coach signed off on?"*) is what produced D127 at all: the orchestrator had extrapolated a placement coach explicitly declined to assert, and `deconflictLegLiftDays` turned out to degrade on a 4-run 5-day week to a fallback putting **squats and calves on the long-run eve and a deadlift the day before the intervals**. He then refused a fix validated on his own calendar (*"not JUST my sunday wednesday off day"*), so the pre-build measure owes a general table at 4-7 training days. Ruled and unbuilt from this session: **D121** (superseded by D125), **D122**, **D123**, **D124**, **D125**, **D127**. §12.
"""
